Z||000000||3fifty||07-10-2001||02:41 AM||||I test fit my wrap around dash yesterday. I had to fight it a little on the leading edge so my Alpine 4x10's would clear the ac duct.<BR>The bottom by the radio pod is about 1 1/4 to far out. I understand that you have to trim the original plastic frame on the console. Do you trim from the front of the shifter to the bottom of the radio pod, or take out the orig pod framework also? Thanks for any input.<BR>3fifty one day!!!!!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||07-10-2001||10:29 AM||||I know of one "professional" install that the dash did not quite fit.  It required lots of trimming to align it properly and was a big PITA. The installer said he'd charge $1000 for the next installation.  The dash looked great once in but the cars owner couldn't get it to fit right, so turned it over.  The PISA door panels didn't quite line up to the mounting holes so they were also a PITA.<P>I think you are experiencing a typical problem with the install.  Measure twice, cut once.  Have lots of patience with the procedure.||||reg||1
